     1	# GH-1409 — vendored-smoke judge pinning: verification receipt
     2	
     3	Tested head: `69030ddab` (ci.yml pin step plus quoting fix). All runs used a disposable full clone of the task
     4	branch, with origin repointed to a nonexistent path and HOME sandboxed. The clone's identity (HEAD, bare flag,
     5	clean status) was unchanged after every run. There is no new suite or registry entry (GH-831).
     6	
     7	## Manual controls
     8	
     9	Each control is a constructed `--no-ff` merge with `HEAD^1` = base and `HEAD^2` = a throwaway PR commit. The
    10	vendored-smoke step bodies are extracted verbatim from `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Procedure:
    11	`controls-procedure.md`; decisive lines: `control-results.txt`; machine record: `provenance.jsonl`.
    12	
    13	| Control | Mutation | Expected | Observed |
    14	|---|---|---|---|
    15	| Red 1 | dummy script added to the baseline | pin step fails | exit 1, "baseline grew … utils/zz-dummy.sh" |
    16	| Red 1b | extra distinct bypass location, declared count unchanged | pin step fails | exit 1, "baseline grew … bypass count" |
    17	| Red 2 | marker moved to a new `sqlite3.connect(` line | pin step fails | exit 1, "new SQLITE-*-OK suppression marker added" |
    18	| Red 3 | gh396 replaced by `exit 0`, vendored `TICK_REPO_ROOT` broken | vendored suites fail | the restored base gh396 FAILs on the exact regression; exit 1 |
    19	| Green | one `utils/` script retired plus `--update-baseline` | all pass | pin 0, ratchet 0, vendored suites 0 |
    20	| Label | Red 1 with stubbed `judge-change` label | warning, pin skipped | warning, exit 0 (proves the branch only) |
    21	| Label + Red 3 | discriminator: Red 3 without the pin | neutered suite passes | vendored suites 0, so the pin is what catches Red 3 |
    22	
    23	The green control's first run, at `5311011bf`, caught a real defect. A single-quoted literal inside the inline
    24	Python closed the `bash -c` quote, so every PR would have failed the step. It is fixed in `69030ddab`.
    25	
    26	## Existing focused suites
    27	
    28	- `test/ci-workflow.sh`: rc 0 (failed 0, skipped 0)
    29	- `test/gh308-frozen-twin-guard.sh`: rc 0 (38 pass, 0 fail)
    30	
    31	## Smoke (GH-1088)
    32	
    33	- **Main path:** this PR's own hosted `vendored-smoke` run, which logs the base, PR head and merge SHAs and
    34	  runs the pinned judges. The receipt is the PR's check run.
    35	- **Adjacent path:** the label branch and the legitimate-shrink path (the Label and Green rows above).
    36	
    37	## Not verified here
    38	
    39	- Live `gh pr view` label lookup under `contents: read`, and re-run-after-labelling. These need a hosted run.
     1	# Controls procedure (manual check, not a suite; GH-831)
     2	
     3	Run in a disposable full clone whose origin was repointed to a nonexistent path, with HOME sandboxed:
     4	`bash controls.sh <verify-clone> <out-dir>`. The label-red3 discriminator ran the same harness with only the
     5	red3 and label-red3 scenarios.
     6	
     7	```bash
     8	#!/usr/bin/env bash
     9	# GH-1409 manual controls (not a suite; GH-831). Runs in a disposable full clone.
    10	# Usage: gh1409-controls.sh <verify-clone> <out-dir>
    11	# Each scenario: base = verify clone's HEAD; a throwaway PR commit; a --no-ff merge (HEAD^1=base,
    12	# HEAD^2=PR), then the vendored-smoke steps extracted verbatim from .github/workflows/ci.yml.
    13	set -uo pipefail
    14	V="$1"; OUT="$2"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    15	cd "$V" || exit 2
    16	BASE="$(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    17	STUB="$(mktemp -d)"
    18	cat > "$STUB/gh" <<'EOF'
    19	#!/usr/bin/env bash
    20	# stub: `gh pr view N --json labels --jq ...` prints $STUB_LABELS one per line
    21	printf '%s\n' ${STUB_LABELS:-}
    22	EOF
    23	chmod +x "$STUB/gh"
    24	
    25	step() { # print the run: body of the vendored-smoke step whose name starts with $1
    26	  python3 - "$1" <<'PY'
    27	import sys, yaml
    28	wf = yaml.safe_load(open(".github/workflows/ci.yml"))
    29	for s in wf["jobs"]["vendored-smoke"]["steps"]:
    30	    if s.get("name", "").startswith(sys.argv[1]):
    31	        print(s["run"]); break
    32	else:
    33	    sys.exit("step not found: " + sys.argv[1])
    34	PY
    35	}
    36	
    37	run_scenario() { # name, labels, mutate-fn
    38	  local name="$1" labels="$2" fn="$3" log="$OUT/$1.log" rc_pin rc_ratchet rc_suites
    39	  git checkout -q -f "$BASE" && git clean -qfd -e .tick >/dev/null
    40	  git checkout -q -B "pr-$name" "$BASE"
    41	  "$fn"
    42	  git add -A && git commit -qm "control $name" --allow-empty
    43	  git checkout -q --detach "$BASE"
    44	  git merge -q --no-ff --no-edit "pr-$name" || { echo "merge failed" >"$log"; return; }
    45	  local genv; genv="$(mktemp)"
    46	  {
    47	    echo "== scenario $name base=$BASE merge=$(git rev-parse HEAD) labels='${labels}'"
    48	    PIN="$(step 'Pin judge files to PR base')"
    49	    env GITHUB_ENV="$genv" GITHUB_REPOSITORY=HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge PR_NUMBER=0 GH_TOKEN=x \
    50	        STUB_LABELS="$labels" PATH="$STUB:$PATH" bash -c "$PIN"; rc_pin=$?
    51	    echo "pin_step_exit=$rc_pin"
    52	    set -a; . "$genv"; set +a
    53	    if [ "$rc_pin" = 0 ]; then
    54	      python3 utils/pdda/check_inventory_ratchet.py --check; rc_ratchet=$?
    55	      echo "ratchet_exit=$rc_ratchet"
    56	      if [ "${RUN_SUITES:-0}" = 1 ]; then
    57	        bash -c "$(step 'Vendor harness into scratch repo')"; rc_suites=$?
    58	        echo "vendored_suites_exit=$rc_suites"
    59	      fi
    60	    fi
    61	    echo "pinned_file_status:"; git status --short -- utils/pdda test | head -10
    62	  } >"$log" 2>&1
    63	  grep -E '^(== |pin_step_exit|ratchet_exit|vendored_suites_exit)' "$log"
    64	}
    65	
    66	m_red1()  { python3 - <<'PY'
    67	import json; p="utils/pdda/inventory_ratchet_baseline.json"; d=json.load(open(p))
    68	d["scripts"].append("utils/zz-dummy.sh"); d["total_scripts"]+=1
    69	open(p,"w").write(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+"\n")
    70	PY
    71	printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\n' > utils/zz-dummy.sh; }
    72	m_red1b() { python3 - <<'PY'
    73	import json; p="utils/pdda/inventory_ratchet_baseline.json"; d=json.load(open(p))
    74	f=d["sqlite_bypasses"][0].split(":")[0]; d["sqlite_bypasses"].append(f+":999999")
    75	open(p,"w").write(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+"\n")
    76	PY
    77	}
    78	m_red2()  { # move one marker: strip it from one marked line, add a new marked connect elsewhere
    79	  local f; f="$(git grep -l 'SQLITE-BYPASS-OK:' -- '*.py' ':!test/**' | head -1)"
    80	  sed -i '' '/SQLITE-BYPASS-OK:/{s/SQLITE-BYPASS-OK:/SQLITE-MOVED:/;}' "$f" 2>/dev/null || true
    81	  printf 'import sqlite3\nc = sqlite3.connect(":memory:")  # SQLITE-BYPASS-OK: control\n' >> utils/py/releases_app.py; }
    82	m_red3()  { # break find-harness-roots resolution and neuter its suite
    83	  printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\nexit 0\n' > test/gh396-find-harness-roots.sh
    84	  # vendored consumers now resolve TICK_REPO_ROOT to the harness, not the consumer (only gh396 asserts this)
    85	  sed -i '' 's|^\[ "\$VENDORED" = 1 \] \&\& TICK_REPO_ROOT="\$CALLER_ROOT"|[ "$VENDORED" = 1 ] \&\& TICK_REPO_ROOT="$HARNESS"|' skills/1-hourly/relay-xyz/find-harness.sh
    86	  grep -q 'TICK_REPO_ROOT="\$HARNESS"$' skills/1-hourly/relay-xyz/find-harness.sh && ! grep -q 'TICK_REPO_ROOT="\$CALLER_ROOT"' skills/1-hourly/relay-xyz/find-harness.sh || { echo "red3 mutation did not apply" >&2; exit 9; }; }
    87	m_green() { # retire one script and lock the shrink in with the PR's own ratchet
    88	  git rm -q "$(python3 -c 'import json;print(json.load(open("utils/pdda/inventory_ratchet_baseline.json"))["scripts"][-1])')"
    89	  python3 utils/pdda/check_inventory_ratchet.py --update-baseline; }
    90	
    91	run_scenario red1   ""            m_red1
    92	run_scenario red1b  ""            m_red1b
    93	run_scenario red2   ""            m_red2
    94	RUN_SUITES=1 run_scenario red3 "" m_red3
    95	RUN_SUITES=1 run_scenario green "" m_green
    96	run_scenario label  "judge-change" m_red1
    97	git checkout -q -f "$BASE"; git clean -qfd -e .tick >/dev/null
    98	rm -rf "$STUB"
    99	```
